'''Wrosidians''' were a semi-[[plant]]-based [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that [[Homeworld|originated]] from the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim's]] [[Wrosdi system]]. The [[humanoid]]s had a set of five organs for [[Atmosphere|atmospheric]] filtering at the back of their head. Members of the species began their life as a bud on a stalk, which resulted in Wrosidian culture not having the same familial and [[gender]] identities found in other cultures, but Wrosidians who budded from the same stalk were considered roughly analogous to relatives. In [[132 BBY]], the Wrosidians [[Bihun]] and [[Basko]] were present in the [[Lomi Usqi Noodle Shop]] on the [[planet]] [[Ueda]] when the [[human]] [[assassin]] [[Mae-ho Aniseya|Mae Aniseya]] [[Indara's murder|attempted]] to [[Death|kill]] the human [[Jedi Master]] [[Indara]] in the establishment.

==Biology and appearance==
Wrosidians were a [[humanoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] of semi-[[plant]]-based beings<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> that [[Homeworld|originated]] from<ref name="Planetnamia" /> the [[Wrosdi system]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]].<ref name="Appendix" /> The method of [[reproduction]] used by Wrosidians involved members of the species starting their lives as buds that grew on stalks. The species possessed a crown of five sensitive organs for [[Atmosphere|atmospheric]] filtering at the back of their head, which were [[Color|yellow-orange]] and darkened at the base.<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> The species had two upper [[limb]]s that ended in three-fingered hands, which gave them enough dexterity to use [[chopstick]]s. In addition, the species had a set of two lower limbs, on which they could stand. Wrosidians were capable of [[Diet|eating]] [[noodle]]s.<ref name="LF" /> The Wrosidian [[Basko]] wore corrugated [[bellow-plates]] that assisted them with breathing.<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

[[File:LomiUsqiNoodleShop-LostFoundDatabank.png|thumbnail|right|260px|Wrosidians Bihun and Basko in the Lomi Usqi Noodle Shop]]
Wrosidian faces featured a pair of [[eye]]s with red sclera and brown irises, with a [[nose]] seated between the eyes. The face also had a [[mouth]] under the nose that enabled them to [[Language|speak]] and contained [[Tooth|teeth]]. Series of vertical slits were located on Wrosidian faces between the nose and the eyes. The [[Alien|non-humans]] lacked visible [[ear]]s. Members of the species had green skin with a purple tint on some parts of their faces&mdash;including around the eyes&mdash;and a brown color on their nose.<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

==Society and culture==
The method of reproduction used by Wrosidians resulted in their culture lacking a direct equivalent of familial and [[gender]] identities found in many other cultures. While Wrosidians who budded from the same stalk were roughly analogous to relatives, their relationship was distinct from that of siblings. Members of the species wore [[clothing]].<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

==Wrosidians in the galaxy==
Wrosidians were a part of [[The galaxy|galactic]] society<ref name="LF" /> by [[132 BBY]]. That [[Standard year|year]],<ref name="Date">{{TheAcolyteDate}}</ref> the Wrosidians [[Bihun]] and Basko&mdash;who originated from the same stalk<ref name="AcolyteVG" />&mdash;were seated at a table in<ref name="LF" /> the [[Lomi Usqi Noodle Shop]] on the [[Planet|world]] [[Ueda]],<ref name="ShopDatabank">{{Databank|lomi-usqi-noodle-shop|Lomi Usqi Noodle Shop}}</ref> eating noodles as the [[human]] [[assassin]]<ref name="LF" /> [[Mae-ho Aniseya|Mae Aniseya]]<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> entered the shop and walked past them on her way to [[Indara's murder|murder]] the human [[Jedi Master]] [[Indara]]. The pair left their place at the table after Aniseya started a fight with Indara's companions.<ref name="LF" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:TheAcolyteVisualGuide.jpg|thumb|right|200px|''Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide'' marked the first identification of Wrosidians.]]
Wrosidians first appeared, albeit unidentified, in "[[Lost / Found]],"<ref name="LF" /> the first episode of the live-action [[Disney+]] series [[Star Wars: The Acolyte|''The Acolyte'']], which aired on [[June 4]], [[2024]].<ref name="EPG">{{SW|url=series/the-acolyte/lost-found-episode-guide|text="Lost / Found" Episode Guide &#124; The Acolyte}}</ref> They were first depicted in a trailer shown exclusively at [[Celebration Europe (2023)|Celebration Europe]]<ref name="Celebration">{{CelebrationTrailer|''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''|Celebration Europe (2023)}}</ref> during the [[Lucasfilm]] Studio Showcase on [[April 7]], [[2023]].<ref name="Studio Showcase">{{SW|url=news/swce-2023-lucasfilm-studio-showcase|text=SWCE 2023: 11 Highlights from Lucasfilm's Studio Showcase}}</ref> The species was identified as Wrosidian in the ''[[Star Wars: The Acolyte: The Visual Guide]]'' reference book written by [[Pablo Hidalgo]], published in [[2025]].<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> They were designed by the creature and droid FX team led by creative supervisor [[Neal Scanlan]].<ref name="Design">{{SW|url=news/the-acolyte-creature-shop-bazil-reveal|text=Inside ''The Acolyte'' Creature Shop: Meet Bazil, the Tynnan Tracker - First Details}}</ref> The scenes in the noodle shop were filmed at [[Shinfield Studios]],<ref name="Fantha Part I">{{WebCite|url=https://www.fanthatracks.com/news/the-acolyte-a-journey-to-the-filming-locations-part-1-madeira|text=The Acolyte: A journey to the filming locations Part 1: Madeira|archivedate=20241204220147}}</ref> [[Wikipedia:England|England]].<ref name="Julian Foddy">{{Lucasfilm|url=news/julian-foddy-acolyte|text=''The Acolyte'' Visual Effects Supervisor Julian Foddy}}</ref> Both Wrosidians were designed and built by [[Tim Berry]] and [[Nicolas Ferrard]], performed by [[Hannah Hornsby]] and [[Caitlin Nicholas]], and puppeteered by [[Wim Oppenheimer]] and [[Patrick Comberford]].<ref name="Tim">{{Instagram|username=timatronics|url=p/C8KyF_CKYZq|name=[[Tim Berry]]|date=2024-06-13|quote=The two noodle creatures - Animatronic design and build by myself and the then animatronic padawan Nicolas Ferrard @obviouslycookies Performed by Hannah Hornsby and Caitlin Nicholas. Puppeteered by Wim Openhiemer and Patrick Comberford.|archivedate=https://archive.ph/PIvlN}}</ref> Concept art of Wrosidians was created by artists [[Barbra Araujo]] and [[Andre Gilbert]] and was subsequently included in ''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Acolyte]]'', a<ref name="Art of Acolyte">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Acolyte]]''</ref> [[2026]]<ref name="Abrams">{{Abrams|url=product/art-of-star-wars-the-acolyte_9781419777349|text=The Art of Star Wars: The Acolyte}}</ref> reference book written by [[Kristin Baver]].<ref name="Art of Acolyte" />

